      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MIKI B NZ (2) took a while to find his feet but now that he has he is proving ultra reliable. Good winning record in recent times and he was as good as ever when 2 metres from the winner in second over 2138m at this track. He can own the speed with the main danger and fancied to get the better of things in the end. That danger is WILLIAMS (1) who has recorded two wins and three minor placings from the past five starts. Performed well once again when third at his latest appearance over 1660m at this track, beaten just 1.4 metres. Will enjoy a nice run from the pole. DREAMALITTLEDREAM NZ (9) is worth another chance after a last-start seventh over 2138m at this track five days ago. LULLABY NZ (7) must be respected after scoring last start by a head at this track over 1660m.",
